      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 800,
        "y": 380
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "The wrong name in the book",
        "description": "At the player's insistence, and over Kell's objection, a child has been taken in for Prout's murder. The Captain will gladly file a murder that embarrasses nobody at court, and whoever really killed Prout is in the clear.",
        "closing": "Narrate the arrest without relish: the accused child's fury or terror, the other one bolting (over the wall or through the gap behind the water butt), and Kell writing her objection down in full. Prout is still turning on the hoist.",
