    {
      "id": "promise-cob-doubt",
      "source": "doubt",
      "target": "doubt",
      "type": "smoothstep",
      "label": "Promise cob doubt",
      "data": {
        "condition": "The player makes Cob a promise that truly answers what he's afraid of, and means it (his name kept out of it, with nothing to the watch and nothing in anybody's book; the men from the loft kept off him; no Mending House; the boots his to keep), or asks him what he knows under a promise like that made before. No dice, whatever they ask with it: he believes it, near enough. He gives up who, in a whisper: Silvertop, the posh cove with the silver-topped cane, the flower smell and a ring with a bit of wheat on it, who comes with the Purveyor's wagons and opens the big doors with his own key; and a big man with a bandaged hand, who said 'Yes, Master'. Asked for a look in his boot as well, he holds the left one out himself.",
        "phase": "outcome",
        "skill": "",
        "dc": 12
      }
    },
