    {
      "id": "bribe-cob-doubt",
      "source": "doubt",
      "target": "doubt",
      "type": "smoothstep",
      "label": "Bribe cob doubt",
      "data": {
        "condition": "The player offers Cob something as the price of a look in his boot, or at what's crackling in it (a coin held up, food, a trade: 'this is yours if I can see what's in there', 'a shilling for a look'), however politely it's asked and whatever they say about the boots staying his, and nothing that answers what he's afraid of. No dice: Cob haggles, boasts, ups the price and takes anything going, but the boot stays on. Bought attention isn't trust, and grown-ups who pay to look at his boots want them off him (the watch, his da, the pawnshop): what's really wrong comes out instead, his way. They're Cob's, and nobody's having them. (Food with nothing asked back is a kindness, not this.)",
        "phase": "outcome",
        "skill": "",
        "dc": 12
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kind-to-cob-doubt",
      "source": "doubt",
      "target": "doubt",
      "type": "smoothstep",
      "label": "Kind to cob doubt",
      "data": {
        "condition": "The player does Cob a kindness with nothing asked back: something to eat, or a dinner stood him freely, with no look at his boots (or anything else) as the price. He takes it with bad grace and a boast, and it counts with him: after it, a polite ask for a look in his boot, the boots staying his, gets a yes.",
        "phase": "outcome",
        "skill": "",
        "dc": 12,
        "establishes": [
